        { "host": "A", "text": "How did they find it?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "An exposed staging server. It was hosting a multi-agent framework Google calls exploit underscore agent, wired into multiple frontier and local models. Google says it compares code before and after patch announcements, identifies potential vulnerabilities, drafts exploits, and executes them without human intervention." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "So the patch itself becomes the lead." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "That's the shape of it. Victim telemetry on the server pointed at French websites in media and entertainment, and the education sector. The configuration files carried Russian-language comments." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Google also says it has independently observed the open-source frameworks CAIRN and PentAGI being deployed, with CAIRN used in intrusion activity against targets including the aerospace sector in the US. All of this is a company claim resting on Google's own telemetry and attribution, and the report offers no independent confirmation." }
